==Battleground==
*15 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~3 seconds<sup>30f~90f</sup>.
*5 [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 3~6 seconds<sup>90f~180f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Nana & Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 6~18 seconds<sup>180f~540f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 6~18 seconds<sup>180f~540f</sup>.
**30 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
**30 [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
**3 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
If you have a wave blocker, this stage is easy, as none of the threats will be able to reach your backline. If you don't, however, then you'll have to deal with what is essentially a Kory. None of the supporting units in this stage make it inviable to use a long ranged attacker, as Master A. is rather slow to move and has an exploitable range. The real problem in this stage are the Otta-Smack-u, capable of pounding any high health units like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] that you might want to use. Thankfully, it is rather easy to grind out the early peons, as long as you have a sufficiently weak enough cat. So, essentially, a long ranged attacker, like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] or [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie]].

